WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.079 --> 00:00:03.200
(upbeat music)

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.920
- Hey, Drew, this is Bashir,

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.030
chef and advocate here in Toronto.

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:08.410
Today I'm sharing with you one

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:10.610
of my favorite and all-time recipe.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.550
It's going to be a beef tartare,

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:14.830
showcasing you the intersectionality

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:16.920
between local food and diversity.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.380
Come along and cook with me.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:19.600
Take some oil,

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.550
adding in to our beets, sprinkling
in a little bit of salt.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:25.380
Make a little bundle

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:26.710
and bake it in the oven

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:28.060
until they become really tender,

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:30.750
approximately 45 minutes to an hour.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.770
So now my beets came of the oven,

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:34.450
allowed them to cool off.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:36.520
I peeled them and with just a box grater,

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:38.720
I just grate them on the larger setting.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.220
Now I'm going to add my butter,

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.090
chopped onions, and at the same time,

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:45.600
we're gonna also add berbere.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.680
This is the staple of Ethiopian cooking.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:48.513
So if you like food

00:00:48.513 --> 00:00:51.080
that has a lot of flavor, aroma

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:53.060
and with a little bit of a heat on it,

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:54.930
berbere, it's the place to go.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:56.800
I'm gonna add my beets,

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.260
a good pinch of salt

00:00:58.260 --> 00:00:59.880
and then I'm going to de-glaze it

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:01.680
with some fresh orange juice.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:04.620
Our beets had the chance to reduce.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.860
There is not more orange juice.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:09.200
So I will take my shiso leaves,

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.100
my injera has been in the oven

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.390
and turned into a crisp,

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:16.160
and I'm going to add a little
bit of the beets on top of it.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:19.150
The best way to really
complement the sweetness

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:21.610
and the heat will be accentuating it

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:23.500
with a little bit of orange zest.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:27.970
Drew, I really hope that you
enjoyed this Canadian dish.

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:31.900
My beets injera shiso with
a little bit of orange.

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:33.649
To the next one, cheers.

00:01:33.649 --> 00:01:36.232
(upbeat music)

